   "readme": "---\nlicense: cc-by-4.0\nlanguage:\n  - he\n  - en\npipeline_tag: text-to-speech\nlibrary_name: piper\ntags:\n  - piper\n  - vits\n  - onnx\n  - hebrew\n  - tts\n---\n\n# Piper Hebrew — noa (medium)\n\nA [Piper](https://github.com/OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl) voice for Hebrew: **noa**, a natural female voice, plus an English\nspeaker (**ljspeech**) in the same model. Fast, CPU-friendly, standard Piper ONNX.\n\nType plain Hebrew — phonemes follow [renikud](https://renikud.github.io) (stressed IPA).\n\n## Files\n\n| File | |\n|---|---|\n| `he_IL-noa-medium.onnx` | Piper voice (ONNX, 22.05 kHz) |\n| `he_IL-noa-medium.onnx.json` | Piper config (`phoneme_type: hebrew`, speakers) |\n| `noa-ljspeech-step20322.pt` | PyTorch checkpoint (generator + discriminator) for further fine-tuning |\n\n## Speakers\n\n| Speaker | Id | Language |\n|---|---|---|\n| `noa` | 0 (default) | Hebrew |\n| `ljspeech` | 1 | English |\n\n## Usage\n\n```sh\necho \"הוא צפה בסרט וראה חיה שצפה במים.\" \\\n  | uvx --from piper-tts piper -m he_IL-noa-medium.onnx -f noa.wav\n```\n\n`phoneme_type` is `hebrew`: Piper converts plain Hebrew to stressed IPA with\n[renikud](https://renikud.github.io), the phoneme convention this model is trained on.\n\n## Training\n\n- **Architecture** — Piper VITS, medium.\n- **Init** — `en_US-ljspeech-medium` (trained from scratch on public-domain LJSpeech), converted to multi-speaker\n  with the speaker conditioning zero-initialized.\n- **Data**\n  - **noa** — 24 h of Hebrew speech generated with [Chatterbox](https://github.com/resemble-ai/chatterbox),\n    Knesset sentences, Whisper-filtered.\n  - **ljspeech** — [LJSpeech](https://keithito.com/LJ-Speech-Dataset/) (public domain), ~24 h.\n- **Steps** — 20,322 (best held-out mel L1 0.405).\n- **Code** — [piper-tts-finetune](https://github.com/thewh1teagle/piper-tts-finetune).\n\n## License\n\nCC BY 4.0.\n"
  },
